User Management Test Cases

User Provisioning & Administration
TC-UM-01: Add New User (Admin / Superadmin)
Given an Admin or Superadmin is on the User Management dashboard,
When they fill in user details (name, email, role) and submit the "Add User" form,
Then the new user account is created, default status is set, and an activation/welcome email is dispatched.

TC-UM-02: Edit User Profile Information
Given an authorized Admin or Superadmin accesses a target user's profile settings,
When they update user fields (e.g., full name, contact info, department) and save changes,
Then the profile updates successfully and changes are reflected immediately.

TC-UM-03: Approve Pending User Account
Given a new user account is created with status "Pending Approval",
When an Admin or Superadmin clicks "Approve",
Then the account status transitions to "Active" and the user receives a confirmation notification allowing them to log in.

Status & Role Changes
TC-UM-04: Block / Deactivate User Account
Given an active user account exists in the system,
When an authorized Admin or Superadmin clicks "Block Account",
Then the account status changes to "Blocked", active sessions for that user are terminated, and subsequent login attempts are denied.

TC-UM-05: Unblock / Reactivate User Account
Given a user account is in "Blocked" status,
When an Admin or Superadmin clicks "Unblock Account",
Then the account status updates to "Active" and login permissions are restored.

TC-UM-06: Designate User as Admin
Given a standard User account exists,
When a Superadmin or authorized Admin changes the user's role to "Admin" and saves,
Then the account permissions update immediately, granting access to Admin-level management features upon their next action/login.

Role Restrictions & System Guardrails
TC-UM-07: Hierarchy Protection – Admin Cannot See Superadmin Accounts
Given a user with the "Admin" role is logged in and views the User List,
When the page renders or user searches execute,
Then Superadmin accounts are hidden completely from the table and search results.

TC-UM-08: Hierarchy Protection – Admin Cannot Edit or Block Superadmin
Given an Admin attempts to directly access a Superadmin profile via deep link or API request,
When the action is initiated,
Then access is denied (403 Forbidden), and no edit, block, or delete actions are permitted.

TC-UM-09: Last Superadmin Guardrail (Role Modification)
Given there is only one active "Superadmin" in the entire system,
When an attempt is made to change this user's role to "Admin" or "User",
Then the operation is blocked, and an error message is displayed: "Cannot change role: System requires at least one active Superadmin."

TC-UM-10: Last Superadmin Guardrail (Account Blocking / Deletion)
Given there is only one active "Superadmin" in the system,
When an attempt is made to block or delete this account,
Then the operation is blocked, and an error message is displayed: "Cannot block/delete the sole remaining Superadmin account."
